duckdb/community-extensions has no standalone JSON Schema file for description.yml to vendor a
copy of — confirmed by inspecting its repository tree and every script under scripts/. The shape
is enforced in code instead, across two scripts:

- scripts/build.py @ 8543f13c6e7f31abda9f6f3caf58a38fcc1fc93b
- scripts/generate_extensions_json.py @ f5544a432f682fe1e7cb6327a49593f34c17acbe

Both commits are the latest touching their file as of 2026-09-04, on duckdb/community-extensions
main @ ae481bd75e850ca5e3e0b32767b0deffc15fa918.

extension.name, repo.github and repo.ref are read by build.py without a .get()/default (via
desc['extension']['name'], desc['repo']['github'], desc['repo']['ref']) — these three are the
only fields that actually break the build when absent, i.e. the real required set. Every other
documented field is read optionally, but not by a single shared script — each is read by
whichever of the two scripts actually consumes it, per field:

  field                          | build.py              | generate_extensions_json.py
  --------------------------------|------------------------|------------------------------
  extension.name                  | required (no .get())  | optional (ext.get("name"))
  extension.description           | not read               | optional
  extension.version               | not read               | optional
  extension.language              | not read               | optional
  extension.build                 | not read               | optional
  extension.license                | not read               | optional
  extension.maintainers            | not read               | optional (defaults to [])
  extension.requires_toolchains    | optional (.get())     | not read
  extension.excluded_platforms     | optional (.get())     | optional
  extension.opt_in_platforms       | optional (.get())     | not read
  extension.custom_toolchain_script| optional (.get())     | not read
  extension.vcpkg_url              | optional (.get())     | not read
  extension.vcpkg_commit           | optional (.get())     | not read
  extension.test_config            | optional (.get())     | not read
  repo.github                     | required (no .get())  | optional (repo.get("github"))
  repo.ref                        | required (no .get())  | optional (repo.get("ref"))
  repo.ref_next                   | optional ('in' check) | not read
  repo.canonical_name             | optional ('in' check) | not read
  repo.andium                     | optional ('in' check) | not read
  docs.hello_world                 | not read               | optional
  docs.extended_description        | not read               | optional

Of the 18 fields that are optional everywhere (i.e. excluding the three required ones above),
9 are read exclusively by build.py (requires_toolchains, opt_in_platforms,
custom_toolchain_script, vcpkg_url, vcpkg_commit, test_config, ref_next, canonical_name, andium),
8 are read exclusively by generate_extensions_json.py (description, version, language, build,
license, maintainers, docs.hello_world, docs.extended_description), and 1
(extension.excluded_platforms) is read by both. build.py alone accounts for exactly half of the
optional-field list, not the near-totality a single-script attribution would suggest — neither
script alone is "where the full optional-field list comes from."

description.schema.json is our own hand-written encoding of the union of both scripts' behavior,
not a byte-for-byte vendored file — re-derive it, and this table, by re-reading those two
scripts (or their successors) if this ever needs updating.
